menu "Motor HAL Configuration"

    config MOTOR_HAL_TIMER_RESOLUTION_HZ
        int "MCPWM timer resolution in Hz"
        default 10000000
        range 1000000 80000000
        help
            The resolution of the MCPWM timer clocks in Hz. Every motor's timer
            uses it; the PWM frequency is a setting of each motor.
            Higher resolution gives finer duty cycle granularity.
            With 10 MHz and 25 kHz, period = 400 ticks (0.25% granularity),
            the default. With 1 MHz it is 40 ticks (2.5%), too coarse for
            the low duty caps of a first motor run.

endmenu
